IL: SPSS Inc</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haro</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Edgell</surname><given-names>ET</given-names></name><name><surname>Frewer</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Alonso</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name><collab>SOHO Study Group</collab></person-group><article-title>The European Schizophrenia Outpatient Health Outcomes Study: baseline findings across country and treatment</article-title><source>Acta Psychiatr Scand</source><year>2003</year><fpage>7</fpage><lpage>15</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1034/j.1600-0447.107.s416.4.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Salize</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Rossler</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The cost of comprehensive care of people with schizophrenia living in the community. A cost evaluation from a German catchment area</article-title><source>Br J Psychiatry</source><year>1996</year><volume>169</volume><fpage>42</fpage><lpage>48</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8818367</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beecham</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Fenyo</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hallam</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Community mental health care for former hospital in-patients: predicting costs from needs and diagnoses</article-title><source>Br J Psychiatry</source><year>1995</year><fpage>10</fpage><lpage>18</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type